      "problem": "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z-1=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-1 & =\\frac{{0}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{2} \\\\ z-1 & =0-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{2} \\\\ z-1 & =-\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{2} \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =-2(z-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives us the equation of the parabola in $yz$-plane.",
